{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wf6Y2g1KxEt4bTP7hHVBdn","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"43a1701e5160cc04f4ea66e7f2bdf4332be6dbb9","date":"2026-10-14T22:35:41+03:00","message":"(feat) Add a text field type for displaying static text in patient registration (#2807)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Herman Muhereza","authorEmail":"hermanmuhereza22@gmail.com"},{"hash":"010e25d0733bdd667c0c676c2a6e4b4ccd138570","date":"2026-10-06T18:01:15+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-6040: Support date person attributes in the registration form (#2809)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Herman Muhereza","authorEmail":"hermanmuhereza22@gmail.com"},{"hash":"1aaae8c003d0ce38c32f07617277398079ccb66a","date":"2026-10-05T08:48:57-04:00","message":"(feat) O3-1830: Allow selecting the preferred patient identifier during registration (#2786)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-1830: Allow selecting the preferred patient identifier during registration\n\n* O3-1830: Deleting the preferred identifier row promotes a fallback\n\n* O3-1830: Guard the preferred option in the Edit mode\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/input/custom-input/identifier/identifier-input.component.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\n\n* O3-1830: apply the suggestions for the screen reader\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.test.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\n\n* O3-1830: address request ordering comments\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/input/custom-input/identifier/identifier-input.component.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* O3-1830: align preferred radio buttons\n\n* O3-1830: The Identifiers section now uses full width when that preferred option is on\n\n* O3-1830: skip the client-side promotion when the user doesn't have the edit privilege\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Cosmin","authorEmail":"cioan@pih.org"},{"hash":"b322ea70dcbc8614774d7b363ca1abca07fe07f0","date":"2026-09-28T19:04:17+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5914: Preserve saved location attributes while searching (#2778)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b4b76423feb220db7e78f27e769f3d32ffaf89b7","date":"2026-09-28T16:06:21+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5916: Reuse generated identifiers when retrying a patient save (#2780)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e7b14cfb17e0871420c4023bb81b19cedcab30b4","date":"2026-09-26T02:37:07+05:00","message":"(fix) O3-5912: Clear dependent address fields when a parent level changes (#2761)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) O3-5912: Clear dependent address fields when a parent level changes\n\n* Remove unused address container providers\n\nRemove the stub registration and resource providers now that address descendants no longer consume them. This prevents future hooks from receiving a no-op setter or empty resources instead of the real context.\n\nUpdate the regression test comment to describe the original failure.\n\n* Simplify the address regression test docblock\n\nDescribe the test setup and assertions without repeating the history of the removed context providers.","authorName":"Faisal Mehmood","authorEmail":"sfm7776@gmail.com"},{"hash":"81c24905675b9e4228681e1d1465497226f8d2d7","date":"2026-09-25T21:10:51+03:00","message":"(BREAKING) Remove offline support from patient management (#2776)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"71b3d3f10534189eafd4786628aeceecdb4a84c2","date":"2026-09-21T22:24:56+03:00","message":"(chore) O3-5924: Use React-scoped JSX types (#2763)","refs":"","body":"Replace global JSX.Element references with React.JSX.Element in registration, service queues and the admission workspace.\n\nPrepare for React 19 types without changing the React 18 runtime or JSX build configuration.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"c14590b98846c7153360116d9823317bdaa22277","date":"2026-09-21T14:53:22-04:00","message":"(fix) O3-5991: Allow post-registration redirects to non-SPA URLs (#2758)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Cosmin","authorEmail":"cioan@pih.org"},{"hash":"0c8915e87db861cc30fa3a40b494ccc8505d2863","date":"2026-09-18T14:42:52-04:00","message":"(fix) Treat a serialized exception from the address hierarchy endpoints as an error (#2757)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"claude[bot]","authorEmail":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"0afed66ac6da680429d7be11f7ebfd360b685405","date":"2026-09-18T12:46:49-04:00","message":"Revert \"(fix) Don't crash the registration form when address hierarchy levels aren't JSON (#2756)\"","refs":"","body":"This reverts commit f84ddd07fecbfb7a99ee72dbe95493aed423f128.\n","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f84ddd07fecbfb7a99ee72dbe95493aed423f128","date":"2026-09-18T08:08:17-07:00","message":"(fix) Don't crash the registration form when address hierarchy levels aren't JSON (#2756)","refs":"","body":"The addresshierarchy module's `getOrderedAddressHierarchyLevels.form` endpoint\ncontent-negotiates: with a browser-style `Accept` header it can answer with a\n200 response carrying an OpenMRS HTML page instead of the expected JSON array.\n`openmrsFetch` parses the body in a try / catch, so that response resolves as a\nsuccess with `data` left `undefined`, and no error is set.\n\n`useOrderedAddressHierarchyLevels` then derived `orderedFields` with no\nfallback, so `AddressComponent` ran `orderedFields.map(...)` on `undefined` and\nthrew during render, white-screening the whole registration form.\n\nGive the derived arrays a fallback and validate the response body in a shared\nfetcher, so a body that isn't the expected array is reported through SWR's\n`error` instead of masquerading as an empty result. The address field\ncomponent's existing `errorFetchingFieldOrder` guard then renders its error\nnotification rather than an address section with no fields.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AikhgxvEhGWfpnA7NXedfZ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"claude[bot]","authorEmail":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"d4d67713e8b9228e90210e122b1054de4f822bd3","date":"2026-09-04T14:20:28+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5917: Keep newly added relationship rows correctly associated (#2721)","refs":"","body":"New relationship rows have no server uuid, so every new row rendered with the same undefined React key and React reconciled them by position. The relationship type select was also uncontrolled (defaultValue). After removing one of two new rows, the surviving row kept showing the removed row's person and type while Formik held the other row's values.\n\nGive each new relationship a client-side id when it is pushed, key rows on the server uuid or that id, and drive the select from its Formik value. The id is never sent to the server: saveRelationships only picks the fields it needs.\n\nThe section test's fetchPerson mock returned a response object where the real function returns an array, so no test could exercise the person search. Fix the mock, add an interaction test that fills two rows, removes the first, and checks the second, and fail any test in the file that logs a React key warning.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ddd67a6674f8dd70f26bd01b36b2ce5d5098e67f","date":"2026-08-24T22:27:05+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5913: Wait for patient data deletions before reporting save success (#2697)","refs":"","body":"* fix: await patient data deletions\n\nWait for name, identifier, and attribute deletions before saving the patient. Propagate deletion failures so the UI cannot report a successful update when cleanup fails. Add regression tests for pending and failed deletion requests.\n\n* test: strengthen identifier deletion coverage\n\nFlush the event loop before checking that the patient save is still pending. This makes the regression test fail against the previous unawaited identifier deletion path.\n\n* chore: remove unused attribute parameters\n\nSimplify the patient attribute payload builder now that deletion handling runs in the asynchronous save stage.\n\n* fix: wait for concurrent requests to settle\n\nWait for every patient-data request to finish before propagating a failure. Add mixed pending-and-failure tests for name, attribute, and identifier operations.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f298c04173e456f92b94fcd90d781c8b89d0e157","date":"2026-08-24T16:45:51+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5919: Clear stale death metadata when marking a patient alive (#2694)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Kavitha Kanchana","authorEmail":"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"29696858ad3a94dff4c3210b6c685208142bbfcb","date":"2026-08-24T16:29:17+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5918: Allow birth and death on the same calendar day (#2692)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Kavitha Kanchana","authorEmail":"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"b62a38834ec4351e7292b9d4d19229eee715e24c","date":"2026-08-24T15:57:44+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5910: Preserve local-language names when editing a patient (#2693)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Kavitha Kanchana","authorEmail":"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"7e67bcc946060d74509c045f2154d936f42d5104","date":"2026-08-24T15:23:59+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5911: Require a non-empty registration encounter type (#2690)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Kavitha Kanchana","authorEmail":"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"2a2048954986bb52b9ff88c2e8a549306076dcea","date":"2026-07-14T20:15:53+03:00","message":"(fix) Request a minimal custom representation in useConceptAnswers (#2622)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Pius Rubangakene","authorEmail":"piruville@gmail.com"},{"hash":"31846e491270d776e2b50c715d48195a71d0a635","date":"2026-06-21T20:43:10+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5488: Unnecessary event listener re-registration in combo-input component (#2323)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Pratik Debnath","authorEmail":"pratikdebnath978@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ec20608aebe7662d3744511e4f9e9491463d9601","date":"2026-06-16T18:19:53+05:30","message":"(chore) O3-5642: Enforce strict equality rule (eqeqeq) across patient management (#2521)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Sathieskumar Sudeshkar","authorEmail":"sudeshkar008sk@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f28d0c90c7c2438f07fb4e0589205dc2209ed6ed","date":"2026-05-14T22:58:25+03:00","message":"(chore) Switch test environment from jsdom to happy-dom (#2534)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5fc0dc3f780ec9c00c40e48e3215b805eca2bc26","date":"2026-05-13T20:23:11+03:00","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#2532)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest across all nine workspace\npackages, aligning patient-management with the patterns adopted\nacross the rest of the O3 apps.\n\n- Root: replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom,\n  and @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and\n  bumped cross-env (7.x to 10.x). Bump @testing-library/dom (9 to 10),\n  @testing-library/jest-dom (6.1 to 6.8), and @testing-library/react\n  (14 to 16) so the /vitest subpath is available. Delete the root\n  jest.config.js.\n- Add a single root vitest.config.ts shared by all packages. Uses\n  jsdom; aliases .scss/.css to identity-obj-proxy via the anchored\n  ^.*\\.s?css$ regex; uses exact-match regex aliases (e.g.\n  /^@openmrs\\/esm-framework$/) for @openmrs/esm-framework and\n  @openmrs/esm-translations so the alias does not capture the\n  /mock subpath; aliases react-i18next to the local __mocks__ file;\n  exposes the tools and __mocks__ paths the way the jest config did\n  via moduleDirectories; pins uuid to the top-level install so\n  esm-offline's nested uuid wrapper doesn't blow up under ESM; caps\n  fakeTimers.toFake so it does not break React's scheduler. Sets\n  process.env.TZ = 'UTC' so the test scripts can drop cross-env.\n- Update tools/setup-tests.ts to load @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\n  and swap jest.* for vi.* across the mocks (single-spa,\n  scrollIntoView, matchMedia, ResizeObserver-as-class).\n- Update every package's test scripts to `yarn run -T vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests` etc. The -T flag tells yarn 4 to resolve the\n  binary from the top-level workspace.\n- Convert the 100+ test files to the vitest API: jest.* swapped for\n  vi.*, jest.Mock and jest.SpyInstance type aliases replaced with\n  Mock and MockInstance from vitest. The many vi.mock(path, () =>\n  ({ ...jest.requireActual(path), override })) factories rewritten\n  as the async vi.mock(path, async () => ({ ...((await\n  vi.importActual(path)) as object), override })) form; the `as\n  object` cast keeps eslint's consistent-type-imports rule happy\n  without per-module type imports. Several vi.mock(name, () =>\n  vi.fn()) factories wrapped in { default: vi.fn() } so the\n  factory returns a module object. vi.mock('@openmrs/esm-framework',\n  () => ({ X })) calls in useWardLocation.test.ts and\n  side-menu.test.tsx rewritten as the importOriginal-spreading form\n  so the partial override does not lose the rest of the framework\n  exports.\n- patient-management/packages/esm-ward-app/mock.tsx: this is loaded\n  as a test fixture by ward-view tests, so its inline jest.mock and\n  jest.fn calls are swapped for vi.mock and vi.fn and a top-level\n  `import { vi } from 'vitest'` is added.\n- Replace two `jest.replaceProperty` usages (in ward-view and\n  admit-patient-form tests) with a small local replaceProperty\n  helper, since vitest has no direct equivalent.\n- Rewrite the IntersectionObserver mock in ward-view.test.tsx and\n  the ResizeObserver mock in tools/setup-tests.ts as ES classes;\n  vitest's vi.fn().mockImplementation(...) is not constructable.\n- Add explicit `import { vi, describe, it, expect, ... } from\n  'vitest'` to test files. Where the field.resource mock uses jest.fn\n  outside a test file, also import vi.\n- Rewrite the xit in appointments/appointment-tabs.test.tsx as\n  it.skip; xit is not a vitest global.\n- Skip one pre-existing field.test.tsx case\n  (`should render AddressComponent component when name prop is\n  \"address\"`) that performs vi.mock inside an it() and relied on\n  the implicit jest.fn return; it never set a return value via\n  mockReturnValue so the component crashed. Flagged with TODO for a\n  follow-up.\n\n692 tests pass across 8 packages (2 skipped). All packages green\nunder tsc; eslint clean.\n\n* (chore) Address PR review: drop jest shims, fix watch script, add coverage thresholds\n\n- Delete the nine per-package jest.config.js files that re-exported\n  the root config. The root config was already deleted by the\n  migration, so these were broken entry points.\n- Update packages/esm-appointments-app's test-watch script (it still\n  pointed at jest --watch --config jest.config.js) to use vitest watch.\n  Other packages were already updated; this one slipped through\n  because its key was test-watch rather than test:watch and didn't\n  match the original migration's perl rewrite. Renamed to test:watch\n  for consistency.\n- Port coverage configuration from the deleted jest config to\n  vitest.config.ts: 80% global threshold and the same\n  collectCoverageFrom restriction to **/src/**/*.component.tsx.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath and document the field.test.tsx skip\n\nTwo follow-ups from review:\n\n- vitest.config.ts relied on new URL(...).pathname for setupFiles and\n  six aliases. On Windows .pathname yields /C:/... which is not a\n  valid filesystem path. Add a fileURLToPath helper and route every\n  URL-based path through it, matching the pattern adopted in\n  openmrs-esm-form-builder.\n- The PR body says the field.test.tsx it.skip is flagged with TODO,\n  but no comment was added. Add one explaining why the test is off.\n\n* (chore) Drop dead @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal alias\n\nvitest.config.ts aliased @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal to\n@openmrs/esm-framework/mock, but no test file in the repo imports\n/src/internal — the alias was copy-pasted from a sibling project\nand never resolved any module here. Remove it.\n\n* (chore) Hoist replaceProperty helper into tools/\n\nward-view.test.tsx and admit-patient-form.test.tsx each carried a\nbit-identical 8-line replaceProperty helper — the local fill-in for\njest.replaceProperty, which vitest does not implement directly.\n\nMove the helper into tools/test-utils.tsx and export it from tools/,\nalongside the other shared test utilities. Both call sites now import\nit from 'tools' like they do for renderWithSwr.\n\nThe helper's behavior is unchanged: it swaps a writable own property\nand returns a {restore()} handle. The body adds a comment noting it\ndoes not handle getter or non-writable descriptors, which jest's\nreplaceProperty does — neither caller relies on that path.\n\n* (chore) Make each app have independently runnable vitest tests\n\nMirrors the pattern Ian introduced for openmrs-esm-patient-chart in\nPR #3301: a single shared vitest config in tools/, a thin re-export at\nthe workspace root, and a thin merge shim per app. With this in place,\n'cd packages/<app> && yarn test' works without bouncing through the\nworkspace root.\n\n- tools/vitest.shared.ts: the actual config that used to live at\n  vitest.config.ts, with the alias and setupFiles paths rebased from\n  './tools/...' and './__mocks__/...' to './...' and '../__mocks__/...'\n  respectively (it now lives one directory deeper).\n- vitest.config.ts: collapsed to 're-export the shared config' so\n  running 'vitest' at the repo root keeps working.\n- packages/*/vitest.config.ts: nine new thin shims, one per app, that\n  do mergeConfig(sharedConfig, {}). Each app now has a discoverable\n  config when vitest is run from inside the app directory.\n- packages/*/package.json: drop the '-T' flag from the test scripts\n  ('yarn run -T vitest run --passWithNoTests' -> 'vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests'); add 'vitest' as a per-app devDependency so the\n  binary resolves under yarn 4 without the workspace-root hop.\n\n692 tests pass across the 8 packages that have tests (esm-home-app has\nnone); 2 skips unchanged.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d3d24812222dc5393068129023fbe748d4184954","date":"2026-04-30T15:26:18+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5534: Replace index-based keys in address suggestions (#2384)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Pratik Debnath","authorEmail":"pratikdebnath978@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":24}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ce8b7a06-4e4c-4716-90ac-774ac6b37a5c","uuid":"a0b2711e-ee75-4938-9764-1c9dea098ea7","timestamp":"2026-10-24T04:13:05.620Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"43a1701e5160cc04f4ea66e7f2bdf4332be6dbb9","date":"2026-10-14T22:35:41+03:00","message":"(feat) Add a text field type for displaying static text in patient registration (#2807)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Herman Muhereza","authorEmail":"hermanmuhereza22@gmail.com"},{"hash":"010e25d0733bdd667c0c676c2a6e4b4ccd138570","date":"2026-10-06T18:01:15+03:00","message":"(feat) O3-6040: Support date person attributes in the registration form (#2809)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Herman Muhereza","authorEmail":"hermanmuhereza22@gmail.com"},{"hash":"1aaae8c003d0ce38c32f07617277398079ccb66a","date":"2026-10-05T08:48:57-04:00","message":"(feat) O3-1830: Allow selecting the preferred patient identifier during registration (#2786)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-1830: Allow selecting the preferred patient identifier during registration\n\n* O3-1830: Deleting the preferred identifier row promotes a fallback\n\n* O3-1830: Guard the preferred option in the Edit mode\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/input/custom-input/identifier/identifier-input.component.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\n\n* O3-1830: apply the suggestions for the screen reader\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.test.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\n\n* O3-1830: address request ordering comments\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/input/custom-input/identifier/identifier-input.component.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* O3-1830: align preferred radio buttons\n\n* O3-1830: The Identifiers section now uses full width when that preferred option is on\n\n* O3-1830: skip the client-side promotion when the user doesn't have the edit privilege\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Cosmin","authorEmail":"cioan@pih.org"},{"hash":"b322ea70dcbc8614774d7b363ca1abca07fe07f0","date":"2026-09-28T19:04:17+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5914: Preserve saved location attributes while searching (#2778)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b4b76423feb220db7e78f27e769f3d32ffaf89b7","date":"2026-09-28T16:06:21+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5916: Reuse generated identifiers when retrying a patient save (#2780)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e7b14cfb17e0871420c4023bb81b19cedcab30b4","date":"2026-09-26T02:37:07+05:00","message":"(fix) O3-5912: Clear dependent address fields when a parent level changes (#2761)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) O3-5912: Clear dependent address fields when a parent level changes\n\n* Remove unused address container providers\n\nRemove the stub registration and resource providers now that address descendants no longer consume them. This prevents future hooks from receiving a no-op setter or empty resources instead of the real context.\n\nUpdate the regression test comment to describe the original failure.\n\n* Simplify the address regression test docblock\n\nDescribe the test setup and assertions without repeating the history of the removed context providers.","authorName":"Faisal Mehmood","authorEmail":"sfm7776@gmail.com"},{"hash":"81c24905675b9e4228681e1d1465497226f8d2d7","date":"2026-09-25T21:10:51+03:00","message":"(BREAKING) Remove offline support from patient management (#2776)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"71b3d3f10534189eafd4786628aeceecdb4a84c2","date":"2026-09-21T22:24:56+03:00","message":"(chore) O3-5924: Use React-scoped JSX types (#2763)","refs":"","body":"Replace global JSX.Element references with React.JSX.Element in registration, service queues and the admission workspace.\n\nPrepare for React 19 types without changing the React 18 runtime or JSX build configuration.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"c14590b98846c7153360116d9823317bdaa22277","date":"2026-09-21T14:53:22-04:00","message":"(fix) O3-5991: Allow post-registration redirects to non-SPA URLs (#2758)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Cosmin","authorEmail":"cioan@pih.org"},{"hash":"0c8915e87db861cc30fa3a40b494ccc8505d2863","date":"2026-09-18T14:42:52-04:00","message":"(fix) Treat a serialized exception from the address hierarchy endpoints as an error (#2757)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"claude[bot]","authorEmail":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"0afed66ac6da680429d7be11f7ebfd360b685405","date":"2026-09-18T12:46:49-04:00","message":"Revert \"(fix) Don't crash the registration form when address hierarchy levels aren't JSON (#2756)\"","refs":"","body":"This reverts commit f84ddd07fecbfb7a99ee72dbe95493aed423f128.\n","authorName":"Ian","authorEmail":"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f84ddd07fecbfb7a99ee72dbe95493aed423f128","date":"2026-09-18T08:08:17-07:00","message":"(fix) Don't crash the registration form when address hierarchy levels aren't JSON (#2756)","refs":"","body":"The addresshierarchy module's `getOrderedAddressHierarchyLevels.form` endpoint\ncontent-negotiates: with a browser-style `Accept` header it can answer with a\n200 response carrying an OpenMRS HTML page instead of the expected JSON array.\n`openmrsFetch` parses the body in a try / catch, so that response resolves as a\nsuccess with `data` left `undefined`, and no error is set.\n\n`useOrderedAddressHierarchyLevels` then derived `orderedFields` with no\nfallback, so `AddressComponent` ran `orderedFields.map(...)` on `undefined` and\nthrew during render, white-screening the whole registration form.\n\nGive the derived arrays a fallback and validate the response body in a shared\nfetcher, so a body that isn't the expected array is reported through SWR's\n`error` instead of masquerading as an empty result. The address field\ncomponent's existing `errorFetchingFieldOrder` guard then renders its error\nnotification rather than an address section with no fields.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AikhgxvEhGWfpnA7NXedfZ\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","authorName":"claude[bot]","authorEmail":"209825114+claude[bot]@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"d4d67713e8b9228e90210e122b1054de4f822bd3","date":"2026-09-04T14:20:28+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5917: Keep newly added relationship rows correctly associated (#2721)","refs":"","body":"New relationship rows have no server uuid, so every new row rendered with the same undefined React key and React reconciled them by position. The relationship type select was also uncontrolled (defaultValue). After removing one of two new rows, the surviving row kept showing the removed row's person and type while Formik held the other row's values.\n\nGive each new relationship a client-side id when it is pushed, key rows on the server uuid or that id, and drive the select from its Formik value. The id is never sent to the server: saveRelationships only picks the fields it needs.\n\nThe section test's fetchPerson mock returned a response object where the real function returns an array, so no test could exercise the person search. Fix the mock, add an interaction test that fills two rows, removes the first, and checks the second, and fail any test in the file that logs a React key warning.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ddd67a6674f8dd70f26bd01b36b2ce5d5098e67f","date":"2026-08-24T22:27:05+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5913: Wait for patient data deletions before reporting save success (#2697)","refs":"","body":"* fix: await patient data deletions\n\nWait for name, identifier, and attribute deletions before saving the patient. Propagate deletion failures so the UI cannot report a successful update when cleanup fails. Add regression tests for pending and failed deletion requests.\n\n* test: strengthen identifier deletion coverage\n\nFlush the event loop before checking that the patient save is still pending. This makes the regression test fail against the previous unawaited identifier deletion path.\n\n* chore: remove unused attribute parameters\n\nSimplify the patient attribute payload builder now that deletion handling runs in the asynchronous save stage.\n\n* fix: wait for concurrent requests to settle\n\nWait for every patient-data request to finish before propagating a failure. Add mixed pending-and-failure tests for name, attribute, and identifier operations.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f298c04173e456f92b94fcd90d781c8b89d0e157","date":"2026-08-24T16:45:51+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5919: Clear stale death metadata when marking a patient alive (#2694)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Kavitha Kanchana","authorEmail":"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"29696858ad3a94dff4c3210b6c685208142bbfcb","date":"2026-08-24T16:29:17+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5918: Allow birth and death on the same calendar day (#2692)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Kavitha Kanchana","authorEmail":"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"b62a38834ec4351e7292b9d4d19229eee715e24c","date":"2026-08-24T15:57:44+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5910: Preserve local-language names when editing a patient (#2693)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Kavitha Kanchana","authorEmail":"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"7e67bcc946060d74509c045f2154d936f42d5104","date":"2026-08-24T15:23:59+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5911: Require a non-empty registration encounter type (#2690)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Kavitha Kanchana","authorEmail":"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"2a2048954986bb52b9ff88c2e8a549306076dcea","date":"2026-07-14T20:15:53+03:00","message":"(fix) Request a minimal custom representation in useConceptAnswers (#2622)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Pius Rubangakene","authorEmail":"piruville@gmail.com"},{"hash":"31846e491270d776e2b50c715d48195a71d0a635","date":"2026-06-21T20:43:10+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5488: Unnecessary event listener re-registration in combo-input component (#2323)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Pratik Debnath","authorEmail":"pratikdebnath978@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ec20608aebe7662d3744511e4f9e9491463d9601","date":"2026-06-16T18:19:53+05:30","message":"(chore) O3-5642: Enforce strict equality rule (eqeqeq) across patient management (#2521)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Sathieskumar Sudeshkar","authorEmail":"sudeshkar008sk@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f28d0c90c7c2438f07fb4e0589205dc2209ed6ed","date":"2026-05-14T22:58:25+03:00","message":"(chore) Switch test environment from jsdom to happy-dom (#2534)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5fc0dc3f780ec9c00c40e48e3215b805eca2bc26","date":"2026-05-13T20:23:11+03:00","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#2532)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest across all nine workspace\npackages, aligning patient-management with the patterns adopted\nacross the rest of the O3 apps.\n\n- Root: replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom,\n  and @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and\n  bumped cross-env (7.x to 10.x). Bump @testing-library/dom (9 to 10),\n  @testing-library/jest-dom (6.1 to 6.8), and @testing-library/react\n  (14 to 16) so the /vitest subpath is available. Delete the root\n  jest.config.js.\n- Add a single root vitest.config.ts shared by all packages. Uses\n  jsdom; aliases .scss/.css to identity-obj-proxy via the anchored\n  ^.*\\.s?css$ regex; uses exact-match regex aliases (e.g.\n  /^@openmrs\\/esm-framework$/) for @openmrs/esm-framework and\n  @openmrs/esm-translations so the alias does not capture the\n  /mock subpath; aliases react-i18next to the local __mocks__ file;\n  exposes the tools and __mocks__ paths the way the jest config did\n  via moduleDirectories; pins uuid to the top-level install so\n  esm-offline's nested uuid wrapper doesn't blow up under ESM; caps\n  fakeTimers.toFake so it does not break React's scheduler. Sets\n  process.env.TZ = 'UTC' so the test scripts can drop cross-env.\n- Update tools/setup-tests.ts to load @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\n  and swap jest.* for vi.* across the mocks (single-spa,\n  scrollIntoView, matchMedia, ResizeObserver-as-class).\n- Update every package's test scripts to `yarn run -T vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests` etc. The -T flag tells yarn 4 to resolve the\n  binary from the top-level workspace.\n- Convert the 100+ test files to the vitest API: jest.* swapped for\n  vi.*, jest.Mock and jest.SpyInstance type aliases replaced with\n  Mock and MockInstance from vitest. The many vi.mock(path, () =>\n  ({ ...jest.requireActual(path), override })) factories rewritten\n  as the async vi.mock(path, async () => ({ ...((await\n  vi.importActual(path)) as object), override })) form; the `as\n  object` cast keeps eslint's consistent-type-imports rule happy\n  without per-module type imports. Several vi.mock(name, () =>\n  vi.fn()) factories wrapped in { default: vi.fn() } so the\n  factory returns a module object. vi.mock('@openmrs/esm-framework',\n  () => ({ X })) calls in useWardLocation.test.ts and\n  side-menu.test.tsx rewritten as the importOriginal-spreading form\n  so the partial override does not lose the rest of the framework\n  exports.\n- patient-management/packages/esm-ward-app/mock.tsx: this is loaded\n  as a test fixture by ward-view tests, so its inline jest.mock and\n  jest.fn calls are swapped for vi.mock and vi.fn and a top-level\n  `import { vi } from 'vitest'` is added.\n- Replace two `jest.replaceProperty` usages (in ward-view and\n  admit-patient-form tests) with a small local replaceProperty\n  helper, since vitest has no direct equivalent.\n- Rewrite the IntersectionObserver mock in ward-view.test.tsx and\n  the ResizeObserver mock in tools/setup-tests.ts as ES classes;\n  vitest's vi.fn().mockImplementation(...) is not constructable.\n- Add explicit `import { vi, describe, it, expect, ... } from\n  'vitest'` to test files. Where the field.resource mock uses jest.fn\n  outside a test file, also import vi.\n- Rewrite the xit in appointments/appointment-tabs.test.tsx as\n  it.skip; xit is not a vitest global.\n- Skip one pre-existing field.test.tsx case\n  (`should render AddressComponent component when name prop is\n  \"address\"`) that performs vi.mock inside an it() and relied on\n  the implicit jest.fn return; it never set a return value via\n  mockReturnValue so the component crashed. Flagged with TODO for a\n  follow-up.\n\n692 tests pass across 8 packages (2 skipped). All packages green\nunder tsc; eslint clean.\n\n* (chore) Address PR review: drop jest shims, fix watch script, add coverage thresholds\n\n- Delete the nine per-package jest.config.js files that re-exported\n  the root config. The root config was already deleted by the\n  migration, so these were broken entry points.\n- Update packages/esm-appointments-app's test-watch script (it still\n  pointed at jest --watch --config jest.config.js) to use vitest watch.\n  Other packages were already updated; this one slipped through\n  because its key was test-watch rather than test:watch and didn't\n  match the original migration's perl rewrite. Renamed to test:watch\n  for consistency.\n- Port coverage configuration from the deleted jest config to\n  vitest.config.ts: 80% global threshold and the same\n  collectCoverageFrom restriction to **/src/**/*.component.tsx.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath and document the field.test.tsx skip\n\nTwo follow-ups from review:\n\n- vitest.config.ts relied on new URL(...).pathname for setupFiles and\n  six aliases. On Windows .pathname yields /C:/... which is not a\n  valid filesystem path. Add a fileURLToPath helper and route every\n  URL-based path through it, matching the pattern adopted in\n  openmrs-esm-form-builder.\n- The PR body says the field.test.tsx it.skip is flagged with TODO,\n  but no comment was added. Add one explaining why the test is off.\n\n* (chore) Drop dead @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal alias\n\nvitest.config.ts aliased @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal to\n@openmrs/esm-framework/mock, but no test file in the repo imports\n/src/internal — the alias was copy-pasted from a sibling project\nand never resolved any module here. Remove it.\n\n* (chore) Hoist replaceProperty helper into tools/\n\nward-view.test.tsx and admit-patient-form.test.tsx each carried a\nbit-identical 8-line replaceProperty helper — the local fill-in for\njest.replaceProperty, which vitest does not implement directly.\n\nMove the helper into tools/test-utils.tsx and export it from tools/,\nalongside the other shared test utilities. Both call sites now import\nit from 'tools' like they do for renderWithSwr.\n\nThe helper's behavior is unchanged: it swaps a writable own property\nand returns a {restore()} handle. The body adds a comment noting it\ndoes not handle getter or non-writable descriptors, which jest's\nreplaceProperty does — neither caller relies on that path.\n\n* (chore) Make each app have independently runnable vitest tests\n\nMirrors the pattern Ian introduced for openmrs-esm-patient-chart in\nPR #3301: a single shared vitest config in tools/, a thin re-export at\nthe workspace root, and a thin merge shim per app. With this in place,\n'cd packages/<app> && yarn test' works without bouncing through the\nworkspace root.\n\n- tools/vitest.shared.ts: the actual config that used to live at\n  vitest.config.ts, with the alias and setupFiles paths rebased from\n  './tools/...' and './__mocks__/...' to './...' and '../__mocks__/...'\n  respectively (it now lives one directory deeper).\n- vitest.config.ts: collapsed to 're-export the shared config' so\n  running 'vitest' at the repo root keeps working.\n- packages/*/vitest.config.ts: nine new thin shims, one per app, that\n  do mergeConfig(sharedConfig, {}). Each app now has a discoverable\n  config when vitest is run from inside the app directory.\n- packages/*/package.json: drop the '-T' flag from the test scripts\n  ('yarn run -T vitest run --passWithNoTests' -> 'vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests'); add 'vitest' as a per-app devDependency so the\n  binary resolves under yarn 4 without the workspace-root hop.\n\n692 tests pass across the 8 packages that have tests (esm-home-app has\nnone); 2 skips unchanged.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d3d24812222dc5393068129023fbe748d4184954","date":"2026-04-30T15:26:18+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5534: Replace index-based keys in address suggestions (#2384)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Pratik Debnath","authorEmail":"pratikdebnath978@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":24}"}],"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Wf6Y2g1KxEt4bTP7hHVBdn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
